BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Galileo
DTSTART:20270319T230000Z
DTEND:20270320T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20261016T232117Z
UID:1007865
DESCRIPTION:<p><em>&nbsp\;Galileo</em>&nbsp\;is the electrifying and explo
 sive new Broadway musical about the man whose discoveries rocked our unive
 rse.<br /><br />When luminary Galileo (four-time Tony Award&reg\; nominee 
 Ra&uacute\;l Esparza) peers into the heavens\, what he sees challenges hum
 anity&rsquo\;s understanding of the world. Unwilling to deny the truth\, G
 alileo finds himself in a fight with the most powerful institution on Eart
 h. As his trusted confidant Barberini (Drama Desk Award nominee Jeremy Kus
 hnier) ascends to power\, friendship leads to betrayal\, and the dreams Ga
 lileo has envisioned for himself and for his brilliant daughter Virginia (
 Tony&reg\; nominee Joy Woods) begin to slip away. Belief\, ambition\, and 
 love pull the trio out of orbit\, each confronting what they&rsquo\;re wil
 ling to sacrifice for what matters most.<br /><br /><em>Galileo</em> tells
  the story of the man whose wonder and curiosity changed the world. Featur
 ing a star-studded creative team\, with a book by Danny Strong (<em>Dopesi
 ck</em>\, <em>Empire</em>) and an original score by Zoe Sarnak (<em>The Lo
 nely Few</em>\, <em>Empire Records</em>) and Michael Weiner (<em>13 Going 
 on 30</em>\, <em>First Date</em>)\, <em>Galileo</em> is directed by Tony&r
 eg\; winner Michael Mayer (<em>American Idiot</em>\, <em>Spring Awakening<
 /em>) and choreographed by Tony&reg\; nominee David Neumann (<em>Hadestown
 </em>\, <em>Swept Away</em>).</p>
LOCATION:Shubert Theatre\, 225 West 44th Street\, New York NY 10036
END:VEVENT
